WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.300
Good morning, John - today,
I'm gonna tell you a bunch of jokes

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.765
that are gonna make you go "har har har" [sarcastically]

00:00:02.865 --> 00:00:03.828
but you - really - you're gonna enjoy.

00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:06.010
You're gonna pretend that you don't enjoy,
but you're gonna like 'em.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.120
I'm planning on beating my previous record;
that will require fifty-two jokes

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.130
 in less than four minutes.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:10.889
Let's go.

00:00:10.989 --> 00:00:13.709
What do you call a five-foot psychic that's
escaped from jail?

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:15.599
A small medium at large.

00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:17.089
Why did the mermaid wear seashells?

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:18.749
'Cause she grew out of her 'B' shells.

00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:20.609
What concert costs forty-five cents?

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:22.585
50 Cent ... featuring Nickelback.

00:00:22.685 --> 00:00:24.760
How did the hipster burn his tongue?

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.205
He drank coffee before it was cool.

00:00:26.305 --> 00:00:28.049
What is invisible, but smells like carrots?

00:00:28.149 --> 00:00:28.484
Rabbit farts.

00:00:28.584 --> 00:00:30.619
What do you call a fake noodle?

00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:31.560
An impasta!

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.300
What do you get when you cross the Atlantic
with the Titanic?

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.270
About halfway.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.240
How does Jack Frost get to work?

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.109
Bi-icycle.

00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:40.149
Bi-icycle.

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:40.989
B'icicle.
[laughs]

00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:43.749
Why did the Face of Boe 
go to the party by himself?

00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:45.379
'Cause he had no body to go with.

00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:47.080
What do you call a fish with no eyes?

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.080
A fsh [still pronounced "fish"].

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.875
When I found out my toaster was not waterproof,

00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:52.470
I was shocked!

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.050
How often do I make chemistry jokes?

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.629
Periodically.

00:00:55.729 --> 00:00:57.259
I actually told one just the other day!

00:00:57.359 --> 00:00:58.389
...There was no reaction.

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:01.399
My boss, he told me to attach two pieces of
wood together.

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:02.489
...I totally nailed it.

00:01:02.589 --> 00:01:04.079
If the mushroom was such a fun guy [fungi],

00:01:04.179 --> 00:01:06.050
why didn't they have the party at his house?

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.220
'Cause there wasn't mush room! 
[laughs creepily]

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.875
Why did Cleopatra fall off the swing?

00:01:10.975 --> 00:01:12.329
Because she's dead.

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:14.199
What's orange, and sounds like parrots?

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:15.069
Carrots.

00:01:15.169 --> 00:01:17.280
The spider just crawled onto my keyboard.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.890
Ookay, I think it's under control.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.910
(Heh, 'cause control is a key...)

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.829
What does Gary Newman want to be 
when he grows up?

00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:25.870
Gary Oldman. [laughs]
Everyone wants to be Gary Oldman, though.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.740
What's Michelle Obama's favorite vegetable?

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.670
Yeah, it's Barackoli [broccoli].
Barackoli, right?

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.090
What are the strongest days of the week?
Saturday and Sunday. 'Cause all the rest,

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:35.940
they're weekdays [weak days].

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.390
What do you call a pretty woman 
on the arm of a banjo player?

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.170
A tattoo.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.295
(I don't know why banjo players. I dunno!)

00:01:42.395 --> 00:01:44.620
My friends and I, 
we put on a performance about puns.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.850
...It was basically just a play on words.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.975
Why do the French only use one egg per omelet?

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.900
Because, in France, one egg is un oeuf [enough]. 
[laughs]

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.595
What did the shy pebble wish?

00:01:53.695 --> 00:01:55.189
Just that she was a little boulder [bolder].

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:56.834
A little boulder! Why is that so cute?

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.779
Did you hear that David lost his ID in Prague?

00:01:59.879 --> 00:02:01.254
Now we just have to call him Dav.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.129
Why was six afraid of seven?

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:06.070
Because seven has cold, dead eyes.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.610
What do you call a pencil without lead?

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.195
Pointless.

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:09.680
Beethoven's favorite fruit?

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.470
Ba-na-na-na [singing, to Beethoven's Fifth
Symphony].

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.305
How do you make an octopus giggle ten giggles?

00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:14.540
You give him ten tickles [tentacles].

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.295
(Ten tickles!) [laughing]

00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:16.250
Knock, knock!

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.110
Who's there?

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.370
Interrupting owl.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.825
Interrupting owl-

00:02:19.925 --> 00:02:20.280
WHO!

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:21.715
Why do gorillas have big nostrils?

00:02:21.815 --> 00:02:22.650
They have big fingers.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.450
Which side of the chicken has more feathers?

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:25.350
The outside.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.290
A horse walks into a bar, 
and the bartender says:

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.560
"Why the long face?"
And the horse says:

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.860
"I'm finally realizing that my alcoholism is
driving my family apart."

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.710
What do you call a man
 who shaves twenty times a day?

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.775
A barber.

00:02:36.875 --> 00:02:38.140
What did one eye say to the other eye?

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.165
"Between you and me, man, something smells."

00:02:41.265 --> 00:02:44.190
Never trust an atom; they make up everything!

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.930
I took the shell off my racing snail, 
'cause I thought maybe

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:46.840
I'd make it a little faster,

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.650
but if anything, it's more sluggish.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.705
Why did the Dalek cross the road?

00:02:50.805 --> 00:02:52.960
To enslave humanity.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.100
What do you call Santa's little helpers?

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.340
Subordinate Clauses.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.785
What did the hat say to the hat rack?

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:58.330
"You stay here, I'll go on ahead."

00:02:58.430 --> 00:02:59.635
Why were the broom late for work?

00:02:59.735 --> 00:03:00.740
'Cus it overswept.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.890
Did you hear? Oxygen and magnesium 
are totally going out.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.015
It's, like, OMg.

00:03:05.115 --> 00:03:06.740
Did you hear that the two antennas got married?

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.590
I heard the ceremony was kind of terrible,
but the reception was awesome.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:10.800
What's ET short for?

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.310
So he can fit on his space ship.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.210
Did you hear about the new corduroy pillows?

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.710
They're making head lines.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.480
My granddad had the heart of a lion.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.950
...and a lifetime ban from the Bronx Zoo.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.920
Sherlock, what do they call 
primary school in America?

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.690
Elementary, my dear Watson.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.760
Why can't you hear a pterodactyl 
goin' to the bathroom?

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:28.510
'Cause the "P" [pee] is silent.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.700
A Golden Retriever and an Irish Setter are
on vacation.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.100
The Irish Setter says to the Golden Retriever,
"Man, I just met two Brazilian dogs."

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.220
And the Golden Retriever is like: "Oh, how,
how many is a Brazilian?"

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.310
How do you cook toilet paper?

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.700
It's easy! You just brown it, 
and then you throw it into the pot.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:41.840
Two whales walk into a bar. 

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.980
One of them is like: "Hmhmhnnnngnbrmuh."
[whale noises]

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:46.665
And the other one is like, 

00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:49.550
"Man, Steve, go home. You are drunk!"

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.250
I wasn't sure it was possible, but here we are,

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.130
fifty-three jokes and four minutes later.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.050
Thank you, everybody on Twitter,
for suggesting jokes for me.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.790
If you want more like this,
I've done a few of these over the years.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:02.290
And John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

